+## 4.1.19 (HexGhoul): quinques in first person move exactly as your body swings them
+
+HexKagune 4.1.19 for Forge 1.20.1. Not tested in game. Previews: `docs/handoff/katana-first-person-4.1.19.png`,
+`docs/handoff/spear-mace-first-person-4.1.19.png`.
+
+Your words: "don't forget the the first person animation, like first person view to match the animation that they got, because they
+currently don't have that."
+
+**What it was:** in first person a quinque was drawn at a fixed spot in front of the camera, tilted by one of three stock motions (a wave, an overhead, a thrust), the same for every weapon and every hit, nothing like what your body did.
+
+**Now:** the katana, the spear, the mace and Dawn are drawn in first person by the same arm, hand, model and transforms as in third person, frame by frame, so every cut in first person is the cut your body makes. The view sits a little behind and to the left of your head, which keeps the weapon right of the crosshair at rest. From the eyes themselves a katana held in chudan points straight along your view and its hilt fills the screen, so that view doesn't work.
+
+- **The katana:** stands just right of the crosshair. The kesa-giri goes up, then down across to the lower left. The gyaku-kesa rises to the right. The yoko-giri sweeps level across the screen. The thrust drives away from you. The finisher sweeps through.
+- **The spear:** points out toward the crosshair, and each thrust pulls back and drives along its line.
+- **The mace:** swings over and down.
+- **The finisher's full-body spin** is left out of first person (the camera doesn't spin with you), but its sweep is there.
+- **Not yet:** the one-handed blade and the launcher keep their old first person for now. The blade gets its own string first; the launcher aims along the crosshair.
+
+### Other
+
+- Protocol 117 (unchanged).
